1. This is a standard **getter method** in Java. Here is a summary of what it does:

### Purpose
The method is used to retrieve the value of an instance variable (field) named `tokenBased` from an object of the class where this method is defined.

### Key Components
* **`public`**: This access modifier makes the method accessible from any other class in the application.
* **`Boolean`**: This is the return type. Unlike the primitive `boolean` (which can only be `true` or `false`), the wrapper class `Boolean` can also return `null`. This is useful if the "token-based" state can be uninitialized or undefined.
* **`getTokenBased()`**: This is the method name, following standard JavaBean naming conventions for retrieving the value of a property.
* **`return tokenBased;`**: This line returns the current value of the `tokenBased` field to the caller.
